-- title:
--   Freeness of 𝒪[[X]] under [p^v]_Φ-substitution
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative ring, $p$ a prime, and suppose $p$ is a non-zero-divisor in $\mathcal O$, the ideal $(p)=\mathrm{span}\{p\}$ is maximal, and $\mathcal O$ is $(p)$-adically complete. Let $\Phi$ be a $d$-dimensional formal group law over $\mathcal O$, that is, a $d$-tuple of power series in the $2d$ variables indexed by $\mathrm{Fin}\,d\oplus\mathrm{Fin}\,d$ with vanishing constant terms, linear coefficients $\delta_{ij}$ in each group of variables, and satisfying associativity under substitution, and assume $\Phi$ is commutative in the sense that each component is invariant under swapping the two groups of variables. Write $k=\mathcal O/(p)$ and let $\bar\Phi$ be the coefficientwise reduction of $\Phi$ along $\mathcal O\to k$. Here `nthSeries` is the iteratively defined multiplication series, with $0$-th term $0$ and $(n+1)$-st term obtained by substituting the $n$-th term and the variables into $\Phi$, so that the $m$-th term is $[m]$. Assume, for some $h$, that $k[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ modulo the ideal generated by the $d$ components of $[p]_{\bar\Phi}$ has $k$-dimension $p^h$. Then for every $v$ there exist $e_j\in\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$, indexed by $j\in\mathrm{Fin}(p^{vh})$, such that every $F\in\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$ is uniquely of the form $F=\sum_j \mathrm{subst}\bigl([p^v]_\Phi\bigr)(c_j)\cdot e_j$ for a family $c_j\in\mathcal O[[X_1,\dots,X_d]]$.
--
--   This is the integral form of Tate's height computation: $\mathcal O[[X]]$ is free of rank $p^{vh}$ over itself via the substitution $X\mapsto[p^v]_\Phi(X)$, the $e_j$ being a basis exhibited through unique expansions. It feeds the freeness statement for quotients of $\mathcal O[[X]]$ by $[p^v]_\Phi(X)-b$, and the proof draws on finiteness over complete rings, miracle flatness for regular local rings, regularity of power series rings over a discrete valuation ring, and the rank computation $\dim_k k[[X]]/([p^v]_{\bar\Phi})=p^{vh}$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_MvFormalGroup_exists_forall_existsUnique_eq_sum_subst_nthSeries_mul_of_finrank_eq_pow.lean

